    skos:definition "Pneumatic Waste Control (PWC) which utilizes a network of underground pipes to transport waste from various collection points to a central location, where it is then processed or disposed of. It uses penumatic suction mechanism.The system requires inspection chamber at certain interval, which must be provided with cover that either easily removable, or provide window for easy inspection." ;
    meta:activationDateUtc "2024-11-11" ;
    meta:classType "Class" ;
    meta:sourceCode "Covering.PWCSINSPECTIONCHAMBERCOVER" ;
    meta:versionDateUtc "2026-03-25" .

