    skos:definition "The landing valve serves as a manual stop valve that allows complete control over the firefighting system. When firefighters need to extinguish a fire, they turn the landing valve handle counterclockwise to activate the water flow. Landing valves are installed on risers within buildings, typically near staircase landings." ;
    meta:activationDateUtc "2024-11-11" ;
    meta:classType "Class" ;
