    skos:definition "A sprinkler control valve is a crucial component in fire protection systems. It’s part of a network that includes sensors, valves, and piping. The valve will activate when the metal strip melts or the liquid-filled glass bulb shatters, allowing the water to escape tfrom the pipe above." ;
    meta:activationDateUtc "2024-11-11" ;
